A<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>0.033<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>1<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>30<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>0.006<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>0.167</div>\r\n\r\n<div>chr1<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>10053<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>+<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>ACCCT<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>0.067<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>2<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>30<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>0.018<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>0.213</div>\r\n\r\n</div><div><br></div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><br></p><div>1. when I plot the % methylation I get a plot that looks like below. </div><div>Is there something wrong with my data?  </div><div>2. when I examine the output of methylRaw object it shows a column with coverage numCs numTs.</div>\r\n\r\n<div>For example the second line from input is shown as </div><div>    chr start end strand coverage numCs numTs</div><div> 1  10016    +   +   +      0.038        0          0 </div><div>Why is numCs and numTs zero?</div>\r\n\r\n<div><br></div><div>Thank you.</div><div><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-39dqZKc42-A/Uz8WkEwbODI/AAAAAAAAABA/Dfhf6Ofu5rQ/s1600/Screen+Shot+2014-04-04+at+4.06.38+AM.png\" style=\"margin-right:1em;margin-left:1em;line-height:18px;text-align:center\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-39dqZKc42-A/Uz8WkEwbODI/AAAAAAAAABA/Dfhf6Ofu5rQ/s1600/Screen%2BShot%2B2014-04-04%2Bat%2B4.06.38%2BAM.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234576204000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3t0CifNjKd1QWeLDeh9gr3\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-39dqZKc42-A/Uz8WkEwbODI/AAAAAAAAABA/Dfhf6Ofu5rQ/s1600/Screen+Shot+2014-04-04+at+4.06.38+AM.png\" border=\"0\"></a><span><font color=\"#888888\"><